  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Teacher Kim and the class go out. They walk to the bookshop. \"Stand in a line,\" says Teacher Kim. Lily is between Mia and Leo. May is behind Leo. \"Don't run in the street!\" \"Cars come here.\" Everyone walks.",
      "They go into the bookshop. It has a lot of books. \"Don't run!\" says Teacher Kim. \"Don't talk. People read here.\" Leo has a big book. He sits on the floor. \"Don't sit on the floor,\" says May. \"It is dirty.\" Leo stands. He smiles.",
      "Teacher Kim has a question. \"How many children are here?\" Lily counts. \"One, two, three, four, five, six.\" \"Seven, eight, nine, ten.\" \"Ten!\" says Lily. \"That is the answer,\" says Teacher Kim. Now they have a new book."
    ],
    "summary": "Teacher Kim takes the class to the bookshop. The children learn what not to do in the street and in the shop.",
